bubbleColumn.rea
-3                     spatial dimension  ( < 0 --> generate .rea/.re2 pair)
1                      number of fields
#=======================================================================
#
#    Tall rectangular column, aspect ratio and BC layout modeled on
#    OpenFOAM's twoPhaseEulerFoam/bubbleColumn tutorial: a narrow
#    liquid-filled column with gas entering at the bottom and free to
#    disengage at the top. See ../eulerEuler.md (or bubbleColumn.par's
#    header comment) for exactly how this deviates from that tutorial.
#
#    x: 0 -> 0.15 m   column width, side walls
#    y: 0 -> 1.0  m   column height (gravity direction), bottom = gas
#                     inlet, top = outflow/disengagement
#    z: 0 -> 0.01875 m, single element, periodic -- pseudo-2D column
#                     (same trick nekRS's other "2D" box cases use: a
#                     periodic single-element-thick homogeneous
#                     direction instead of OpenFOAM's empty/frontAndBack
#                     patch pair)
#
#    Run `genbox` on this file (Nek5000/tools/genbox) to produce
#    bubbleColumn.re2 -- it is intentionally NOT checked in, unlike
#    examples/eulerEulerTemplate/'s reused placeholder mesh, since a
#    wrong-geometry mesh here would misrepresent the case.
#
#=======================================================================
#
Box
-8 -48 -1              nelx,nely,nelz for Box
0 0.15 1               x0 x1 ratio
0 1.0  1               y0 y1 ratio
0 0.01875 1            z0 z1 ratio
v  ,v  ,v  ,O  ,P  ,P   BCs (3 characters each!) x0/x1=side walls, y0=bottom (gas inlet, see udfDirichlet), y1=outflow/top, z0/z1=periodic
